<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · British Isles</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Mide</h1><p class="st-meta">550 CE – 1173 CE (approx.) · capital Uisnech</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The midland kingdom around the sacred hill of Uisnech, ruled by the Clann Cholmain kings who often held the kingship of Tara.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Mide formed in the 6th century as the southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ui-neill">Ui Neill</a> dynasties established themselves in the Irish midlands. The Clann Cholmain branch, descended from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/colman-mor">Colman Mor</a>, emerged as its dominant line by the 8th century, ruling in what is now <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/county-westmeath">Westmeath</a> with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hill-of-uisneach">Uisnech</a> as its symbolic centre.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Clann Cholmain kings alternated the kingship of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hill-of-tara">Tara</a> with the northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ui-neill">Ui Neill</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mael-sechnaill-mac-maele-ruanaid">Mael Sechnaill mac Maele Ruanaid</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mael-sechnaill-mac-domnaill">Mael Sechnaill mac Domnaill</a> were among the most powerful kings in Ireland. The kingdom contained great monasteries such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/durrow-abbey">Durrow</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/clonard-abbey">Clonard</a>, and royal sites at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lough-ennell">Lough Ennell</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brian-boru">Brian Boru's</a> rise, Mide was repeatedly partitioned by rival provincial kings. In 1172 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-ii-of-england">Henry II</a> granted it to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hugh-de-lacy-lord-of-meath">Hugh de Lacy</a>, creating the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/lordship-of-meath">Lordship of Meath</a>, and the native line survived only as minor lords.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/kingdom-of-mide.jpg" alt="Kingdom of Mide" width="320" height="417"><figcaption>Image: Erigena · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kingdom_of_Mide-900.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>550 CE – 1173 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Uisnech</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Mael Sechnaill mac Maele Ruanaid, Mael Sechnaill mac Domnaill</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Old and Middle Irish</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/ireland">Ireland</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Mide, Meath, Clann Cholmain</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=862&amp;focus=kingdom-of-mide" aria-label="Kingdom of Mide on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4533 336 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Mide lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M4853 592L4849 593M4853 592L4856 589"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M4849 593h0M4856 589h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4853 592h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4853 592h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=862&amp;focus=kingdom-of-mide">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
